// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : scripts/SpawnDefs/InfoNPCs/_src/Arena_Info_NPC.xls 	Sheet : ArenaInfo_Galaxy 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 37 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1517267954" "<em=lecture f=a>Hey there, and welcome to the Galaxy City Arena! Are you ready to rumble?<em none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3494604015" "<em=clipboard f=a>Taking signups for the next round here!<em=none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2355952554" "<em=lecture f=a>Wanna sign up? I'll show you how to create or join matches.<em=none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1408292778" "<em=lecture f=a>Having trouble getting started? Come talk to me, and I'll show you how to use the terminals!<em=none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1505643167" "<em=lecture f=a>When you are ready for your match, don't forget to stop by our stores for that last minute inspiration!<em=none>"
// Script Variable RestrictedText :
"P3648341633" "Beat it, I'm busy."
// Script Variable InfoText :
"P1849145586" "Welcome to the Galaxy City Arena! In this exclusive venue, you can challenge your fellow heroes for a match! You can have one of several kind of matches, but for now, let's focus on getting you into the game!<br><br>You will notice several grey and blue 'Battle Terminals' near the walls all around the Arena. Simply walk up to one, and click on it.  This will bring up the <b>Arena Interface</b>. From here, you can do one of two things: start a match, or join a match.<br><br><b>Creating a match </b>- Click the 'Create Event' button. This will bring the match-up window. In the upper left corner of the window, select your game type, be it a Gladiator match, Pentad, or a Custom match. Select how long you want the battle to run, and what level ranges you will allow to enter your game. To increase or decrease the amount of people you wish to have in your game, simply adjust the center slider near the top of the window. Once these settings are made, click the green <font color=green>'List Event'</color> button at the bottom left corner of the window. If you wish for this match to be made private, and not seen in the match listings, simply select 'Invite Only', right above the 'List Event' button, however you will need to manually invite players into your matches by either typing '/arenainvite [playername]', or right-clicking your challenger and selecting 'Invite to Arena Event'.<br><br><b>Joining an event </b>- Simply highlight the match you wish to join, and click the 'Join Event' button. That's it, you're in the match! This will open the match-up window as if you were creating an event, however in this case, you will not be able to change the game settings, only the event creator will be able to modify them.<br><br>For more information on our game types, please visit the Games Information Agent located here in the Arena."
// Script Variable OutLoudInfoText :
"P1001925780" "<em=clipboard>"
// Script Variable Leave :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// DisplayName for N_NPC :
"P2021116694" "Arena Information Agent"

// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************

